    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is heavily anchored by the favorable matchup against Ryan Feltner, whose 4.56 xERA provides a significant ceiling for our roster. **Tyler Freeman** (72.83) and **Bryson Stott** (72.62) lead the offensive projections; **Stott** is particularly well-positioned to capitalize on his dynamic platoon advantage against the volatile Roki Sasaki, while **Freeman** benefits from a premium spot in the order and a park factor boost. **Matt Chapman** (70.06), **Daulton Varsho** (69.94), and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) round out the top tier of starters. Notably, **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Drew Gilbert** are active specifically because the slow delivery from the opposing battery creates an ideal environment for their aggressive base-stealing profiles, which remains a priority for our strategy in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who produced a 46.58 but ultimately failed to displace **Lawrence Butler** or **Jeremiah Jackson**. While **Sheets** offered reasonable value, the risk associated with a sub-4.00 xERA arm in Griffin limited his upside compared to our starters facing more hittable pitching. Conversely, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is active with a 57.26 despite a modest projection; he is fighting a slight headwind in BvP history against Sonny Gray, but his daily floor is too high to justify benching him. **Will Smith** (40.42) remains our most precarious start as he narrowly cleared our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold; we are tracking his lineup status closely, as any drop in the order against Jes\u00fas Luzardo would likely result in a benching to preserve our limited game caps.",
